  "intro": [
    "Every RDS operation the emulator advertises, and what Emuplane does with it.",
    "The control plane is the Query API (`Action=…`, XML answers) signed with the",
    "`rds` credential scope, and has no console action.",
    "The emulator can back an instance or cluster with a real Postgres/MySQL container",
    "when Docker is available; without it — the usual case, and the one the tests run",
    "against — every resource is a control-plane record that provisions `available`.",
    "A stable instance, cluster, snapshot, group and proxy carry the read, modify and",
    "tag rows; delete and lifecycle actions make their own resource. Global clusters",
    "span two regions under one account so switchover and failover have a secondary",
    "to promote.",
    "One wire-shape caveat: the emulator wraps each global cluster in",
    "`<GlobalClusterMember>` in `DescribeGlobalClusters`, where the service model",
    "expects `<GlobalCluster>`, so a botocore client parses an empty list even though",
    "the clusters are there; the coverage test reads the raw XML."
  ],
